  "Number": 3,
  "Question": "Alicia earns \\(\\$20\\) per hour, of which \\(1.45\\%\\) is deducted to pay local taxes. How many cents per hour of Alicia’s wages are used to pay local taxes?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(0.0029\\)",
    "B": "\\(0.029\\)",
    "C": "\\(0.29\\)",
    "D": "\\(2.9\\)",
    "E": "\\(29\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "Convert the tax percentage to a decimal:\n\\[\n1.45\\%=\\frac{1.45}{100}=0.0145.\n\\]\nMultiplying the hourly wage by this fraction gives the tax in dollars per hour:\n\\[\n20\\cdot0.0145=0.29.\n\\]\nSince one dollar is \\(100\\) cents, \\(0.29\\) dollars is \\(\\boxed{29}\\) cents. The answer is choice \\(\\text{E}\\).",
